# K03 NS-ROLES-CALL (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-CALL-20261007-17; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md:668): with Model existing,
# `Model: args` is Model's call whatever the actuals are -- an ordinary named Structure takes none: refused at the
# call, by the call's own arity check, never a declaration of an unknown actual.
# In a named body: Outer retains an application of Model, the first actual unknown.
int: hits 0
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
end: Model
Outer:
    int: extra 1
    Model: zz extra
end: Outer
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
